#ASSERT `s 899(1A) section 899(1) is subject to section 899A` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 899(1A) section 899(1) is subject to section 899A` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 899(2): as s 896(2); the administrator limb also covers a company in relation to which an administration order is in force
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) the company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) a creditor of the company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) a member of the company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; a person named only on a condition whose condition is not met is not covered, not barred: an unmet "if" on a power the text gives answers NOTHING (name-test sweep, fork F28)
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) the liquidator of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` `s 896(2) the administrator of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
